<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Laneset's default (en) words.

  This file holds two things and no third. The **preserved** keys are the ones the app shell owns and
  this screen only reads: the app's identity, the host's placeholder for an empty detail pane, the
  About surface and the Settings surface. The **home** keys are this screen's own vocabulary — the
  constraints form, the generated session, the runner and the handoff — and they are the product's
  own words.

  Three rules hold across the block, and each is a defect that already happened once somewhere in this
  factory:

  - **Every user-facing word is here, never in Kotlin.** A literal is a string a translator cannot
    reach and `scripts/core/localization.mjs` reports it.
  - **The Russian tree carries the same keys with the same format arguments.** Android merges every
    file in values/ into one table and `scripts/core/policy.mjs` compares the two trees in both
    directions, so a key or an argument in one and not the other is a failure rather than a fallback.
  - **Every placeholder is positional.** A bare percent is read as a defect wherever the string is
    formatted, so the copy uses forms like the first and second argument by number.

  The numbers in the block are the pool's own: metres, whole minutes, and times as a pace clock reads
  them. A stroke or a piece of gear is lower case because it is read mid-sentence in a set line.
-->
<resources>

    <!-- The app's identity. The store title lives in naming.json; this is the same carrier, and the
         app_idea line is the one this screen does not rewrite. -->
    <string name="app_name" translatable="true">Laneset: Swim Set Builder</string>
    <string name="app_idea" translatable="true">A swim set builder that computes each session from the swimmer\'s own constraints (minutes, pool length, focus, strokes to avoid, gear on deck) against authored programming rules, walks them through the two pace trials that put a target time on every interval, and prints or shares the set list; one-time unlock, offline, no account.</string>

    <!-- Read by ui/PlayKilnApp.kt for the empty detail pane beside Home. Not this screen's key, and
         not renamed: another worker reads it, and deleting it breaks the host. -->
    <string name="home_pick_section" translatable="true">Choose a section to open it here.</string>

    <!-- Home's top bar and identity header. The header repeats the carrier beside the one sentence
         that says what the app does, and the top bar carries it alone at its own width. -->
    <string name="home_title" translatable="true">Laneset</string>
    <string name="home_tagline" translatable="true">Swim sets built from your own constraints.</string>
    <string name="home_about_action" translatable="true">About</string>

    <!-- Before anything is built. The empty state has to sell the first build without a price on it:
